  "reason": "The current best (config_042, acc 0.599) uses pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat. The main remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder can outperform PCA while keeping all other best-performing components fixed. config_048 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable test of the RNA encoder. scgpt was poor (0.494) but with resnet50; scvi_n200 is a lighter, more standard VAE-based encoder that may capture biological structure PCA misses without scgpt's instability. If it matches or beats 0.599, we have a strong new best; if it underperforms, we confirm pca_n2000 as optimal and can focus remaining budget on fusion/aggregation refinements. Expected cost: moderate (~6–8 GPU hrs), since scvi_n200 adds encoder training overhead over PCA but is substantially lighter than scgpt (which added ~5.5 hrs). This is the highest-information experiment given 4 remaining slots: it either opens a new promising direction or locks in the RNA encoder choice so later experiments can target other knobs."
